  <p>
    <strong>After bitcoin prices dipped to a low of $30,066 per unit last week, lots of people have been focused on the panic sellers. Meanwhile, when bitcoin prices plunged, the number of bitcoin addresses in accumulation tapped an all-time high at 545,115 addresses.</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 class="jeg_post_title" style="text-align: center;">
    Number of Bitcoin Accumulation Addresses Hit New Highs
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Bitcoin (BTC) prices slid from a $64,895 per unit high to a low of $30,066 per bitcoin in 30 days losing more than 53% in value. When the price plunge took place data from Glassnode’s bitcoin “accumulation addresses” spiked.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    The number of bitcoin addresses in accumulation shows fundamental strength signals and gives investors a perspective of long-term holders. Glassnode’s data reflects addresses with little to no incoming transactions, as opposed to addresses that are more active.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-461673 size-full" title="Data Shows Bitcoin Addresses in Accumulation Captures Fresh New Highs" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53.jpg" alt="Data Shows Bitcoin Addresses in Accumulation Captures Fresh New Highs" width="2416" height="1316" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53.jpg 2416w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53-300x163.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53-1024x558.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53-768x418.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53-1536x837.jpg 1536w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53-2048x1116.jpg 2048w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53-696x379.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53-1392x758.jpg 1392w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53-1068x582.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53-771x420.jpg 771w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-tue_25_may_13_07_53-1920x1046.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2416px) 100vw, 2416px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Nine months ago, Glassnode reported on accumulation addresses reaching the 500k mark. “There are over 500,000 Bitcoin ‘accumulation addresses’ holding a total of 2.6 million BTC (~14%). Accumulation addresses: – have 2+ incoming txs – never spent BTC – were active in the past 7 years (accounting for lost coins) – exchanges & miners are excluded,” the analytics firm said at the time.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    The current number of bitcoin addresses in accumulation recorded on Monday, May 24, 2021, was approximately 545,115 addresses, according to Glassnode stats.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-461674 size-full" title="Data Shows Bitcoin Addresses in Accumulation Captures Fresh New Highs" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1.jpeg" alt="Data Shows Bitcoin Addresses in Accumulation Captures Fresh New Highs" width="1800" height="1013" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1.jpeg 1800w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-300x169.jpeg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-1536x864.jpeg 1536w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-696x392.jpeg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-1392x783.jpeg 1392w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-1068x601.jpeg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-746x420.jpeg 746w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-190x107.jpeg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-380x214.jpeg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-760x428.jpeg 760w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-1520x855.jpeg 1520w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image1-1280x720.jpeg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Glassnode’s “The Week On-Chain” highlights “anecdotal indicators” from Bixen’s Mustafa Yilham recent tweet storm that alluded to miner sell pressure stemming from China.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    “Observing the spending of miner coins demonstrates that whilst there is an uptick in miner-to-exchange flows,” Glassnode’s report notes. “Up from 100 BTC/day to 300BTC/day, this still represents a relatively small portion of the ~900BTC/day issuance,” the researchers said.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    More than 16,000 addresses have been added to the sum of bitcoin addresses in accumulation since the first week of May. Following the dip to $30,066, bitcoin addresses in accumulation jumped higher.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <strong><em>What do you think about the</em> number of bitcoin addresses in accumulation stats? Let us know what you think about this subject in the comments section below.</strong>
  </p>
